-- checkpoint). after the finish, or a catch, the map starts again, and the farm carries on.
-- v17: a fence costs a knock hit of at most 6 st/s, so it is taken at full speed (PassSpeed 140, was 55, which slowed the car for every
-- roadblock). fences cost 40 (was 10), so a clear lane near a fence is taken. corner slip thresholds 9 and 4.5 degrees (the drift assist starts at 9).
-- v16: checked against the newest library (adda5aa): the names the script calls are all there, the config addon and the ESP
-- module keep their functions. a startup check names any library function this script needs that a later update removed.
-- v15: the library's config addon (addons/Config.luau) is loaded after the library, so the Configs tab, the autoload and the
-- share codes exist again. Every saved control has a Flag, so the config holds the driver and the ESP settings.
-- v14: the driver checks a lane change along its path (a solid thing it would meet while moving over is costly), steers with a Stanley
-- law (heading error plus the sideways error), stops for a solid thing instead of creeping into it, caps fence hits at 55 st/s,
-- and keeps the measured braking under the car's own. the UI uses the new library's names (Default, Placeholder, its Configs tab).
-- v13: the teleport runs from a queue, inside a hook on CarInput.Read, in the physics step. the finish is crossed by the game's own lineStep.
-- v12: teleport run (each checkpoint in turn, then the finish line through LineCross) and next-checkpoint jump, in the Assist tab.
-- the Server mile status shows what the server counted, so a jump the server rejects shows up as a number that does not move.
-- v11: every tag shows what it is, its live distance from the car in studs, its side, and for a road marker the time to it.
-- monsters show their State when the game gives one. new route markers: avalanche spots and pads, read from the world config.
-- v10: a knock model that is a body (wreck, van) is a solid thing, a cone stays soft, the sweep starts 10 studs behind the car,
-- and the status shows the solid thing in the lane the car will take.
-- v9: every collidable part ahead is found by a sweep (not a list), cars and monsters are tracked every frame with their
-- velocity, obstacles are met at the time the car reaches them, and the car follows a slower thing ahead instead of stopping.
-- v8: obstacles have three kinds. solid (wrecks, other cars, monsters) is avoided and crept past, pits stop the car, and
